Title: Fold gaze into review-pr: one review skill, the gate keys on a review on the head
Created: 2026-10-21
Author: reviewer

--- log ---
2026-10-21T13:24Z reviewer created

--- body ---
## Context
At the author's request on 2026-10-21 ("do we even need the gaze skill?"). `/gaze`
orchestrates three other things: `/review-pr` (the seats), `/verify-adherence`
and the runtime's own simplify. What it adds: one entry point; the head anchor;
one result comment (REVIEWED, FINDINGS or ESCALATE, with a `next:` line) that
`/verify-gate` requires for the head; the 15-file un-reviewable breaker with its
waiver; a fork contract; cleanup of the review worktree; and the never-APPROVED
property pinned by `tests/test_gaze_never_approves.py`.

Cost seen on 2026-10-21: nested forks that could not launch seats, a duplicate
run colliding with one in flight, escalations for a degraded panel, about three
gaze runs per pull request since PR 1550, and 48 KB of text across `SKILL.md` and
five references. The findings came from the review-pr seats. On `main`, `gaze`
appears in 15 files under `skills/`, 7 under `scripts/`, 2 under `rules/` and 33
under `tests/` (67 under `docs/`, which stay as history).

Author stance, decided the same day: trust the orchestrator (no floor, no
category; it picks seats and tools, may use its runtime's own verify and simplify
or none, and is told it has the external reviewer tools); always verify (the gate
rules; the integration check on the merge candidate); monitor (journal, sweep,
runs per pull request). Ticket 1176 deletes the width, depth, scoping and risk
machinery first.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Fable's review of the fold is recorded in the ticket log (the smallest
      version, what is lost, the one risk that would say don't), and the decision
      to fold or keep is written down with the author's name on it.
- [ ] If folded: `/review-pr` carries the surviving rules in a few lines: the head
      anchor, the 15-file breaker and its waiver, the never-APPROVED rule, the
      DEGRADED and retry-once lines, and the result contract the gate reads.
- [ ] `/verify-gate` keys on a review on the head, not on a gaze result; raid
      phase 6, merge and hunt call the review skill directly. Adherence stays its
      own skill; simplify stays a runtime tool the orchestrator may use or skip.
- [ ] `skills/gaze/` is removed, with its fork contract, output template and
      cleanup file; `tests/test_gaze_*` are deleted or moved to the surviving
      skill; the never-APPROVED test keeps its frozen allowlist.
- [ ] A grep for the old name across `skills/`, `scripts/`, `rules/` and `tests/`
      is empty; `docs/` keeps history. Catalog regenerated; drift check clean.
- [ ] The run count per pull request over the next 20 is recorded against the
      2026-10-21 figure of about three.
- [ ] Nothing here requires a particular agent runtime.
